where $\mathcal{D}_{n} := \mathcal{D}(\bm{\theta}_{n}, \bm{w}_{n})$, $\bm{d}_n^D := \bm{d}^D (\bm{\theta}_{n}, \bm{w}_{n})$, and $\mu > 1/4$. The sequences $(\beta_n^G)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ and $(\beta_n^D)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ defined by [REF:CG_G_dim] and [REF:CG_D_dim] satisfy (C2) and (D4). Property [REF:R_1] ensures that the CG-type algorithm has the the same convergence rate as in (I).

